R-UM1 R-P6 R-EF1 R-PP4 R-LD2 (slice 032b gap test: E4, E5, mutation u2 of the code agent): the baseline of the project explains one of 2 failing modules, and the app imports none of them. 1 run of `update json` on 1 project (p1: acme/pf 0.1.0, acme/json 2.0.0 moves to 2.1.0, acme/parser 1.0.0, no import of a parser module). The fixtures are the ones of run 1 of `probe/un1-units`: the unit check of acme/parser on nightly-2026-10-08-0a1b2c3 fails in Parser.roc and in Yaml.roc (`fx/units`, the fixture `unit-fail-two`), and the baseline has an error in Parser.roc of the same package (`fx/probes`, the fixture `pkg-base`).
The unit fail has 2 modules. The baseline explains Parser.roc (R-P6), so only Yaml.roc is ignored: the one note `note: module Yaml fails on nightly-2026-10-08-0a1b2c3. Your app does not import it.` follows the build line. There is no note for Parser (the error is the error of the baseline, the old line `note: unchanged error` has it). With an empty baseline in `UnitFlow.verdict!` the scan would give a second note for Parser, and this case would see it.
The calls after the facts: round 1 (the baseline and the 3 unit checks), one `db_write` of the facts, round 2 (the check of the candidate, the same error as the baseline), round 3 (the build). The app imports no module, so the scan of the used modules has nothing to read and makes no `read_files` call.
